<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Xanthippus (father of Pericles)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 490s–<a href="/years/479-bce">479 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Xanthippus was an Athenian statesman and general, the father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pericles">Pericles</a>. Ostracised in 484 BCE, he was recalled during <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xerxes-i">Xerxes</a>' invasion and commanded the Athenian contingent at the victory of Mycale in 479 BCE. He then besieged and took Sestos on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hellespont">Hellespont</a>, the episode with which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> ends his Histories.</p></div>
